-- The demo world (design plan §2, §4): clients, the fleet, the crews, the missions, the
-- cargo in bond, and the telemetry. Every §7 condition keeps at least one row on each side,
-- and every paged list is deeper than its default page. Names avoid apostrophes: Spanner DML
-- does not accept a doubled quote inside a string literal.
--
-- A person is named by the id of their account, never by their username, which may
-- change: the cast's accounts are created by the bootstrap under fixed ids
-- (cmd/bootstrap/users.json), with one prefix per users table as the rows here take one
-- per table, and numbered in the file's order. Every column that anchors a person
-- (UserId, PilotUserId) or records who did something (BookedByUserId, FiledByUserId, AwardedByUserId,
-- OpenedByUserId) holds that id, and the name column beside each of the latter (BookedByName
-- and the others) holds the person's username as it was when the row was written, which
-- is what a page shows.
--
-- The crew's accounts, f0000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000NN: 01 governor, 02 marshal,
-- 03 cadet, 04 pilot, 05 veteran, 06 lead, 07 dispatcher, 08 overseer, 09 booking,
-- 10 wingco, 11 engineer, 12 quartermaster, 13 supercargo, 14 salvor, 15 yeoman,
-- 16 purser, 17 registrar, 18 photographer, 19 archivist, 20 assessor, 21 hazards,
-- 22 dock, 23 watch, 24 harbormaster, 25 adjutant, 26 surveyor, 27 rigger, 28 bosun,
-- 29 droid-r7 (the service account). The members' accounts, the portal's people,
-- f1000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000NN: 01 client (Client Cleo of Halvard Freight),
-- 02 surveyor (Ines Marrow of the Meridian Survey Office, who is not the crew's surveyor:
-- the same username in two auths is two people).

-- Insured (salvage cover) takes all three states across the four clients: Halvard
-- confirmed, Meridian and Bastion Relay still unknown, Vellum declined.





-- Commendations are the commendations desk's rows, the one resource behind a feature flag
-- (pkg/resources/features.go): Pax carries two citations and Vela one, so a card counts them
-- once the flag is on, and the desk lists them newest first.


-- Callsigns (a nullable ARRAY<STRING(16)> column typed by the plain slice) take both
-- answers and the absence of one: Hammer has filed its two, Portcullis flies silent and
-- says so with an empty array, and Tongs and Ashfall have not filed yet, so the column is
-- NULL there and the row carries a null.



-- Two haulers carry cargo bays (an ARRAY<INT64> column, number[] in the console); every
-- other ship takes the column's default, an empty array.









-- Briefing templates are a catalog served from Go (pkg/computedresources), so the column
-- holds an identifier the schema knows nothing about; three Anvil missions name one.
UPDATE Missions SET BriefingTemplateId = 'standard' WHERE Id = '80000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001';
UPDATE Missions SET BriefingTemplateId = 'hazard-first' WHERE Id = '80000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003';
UPDATE Missions SET BriefingTemplateId = 'client-facing' WHERE Id = '80000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004';
